A||||5||fiero56||Getrag-Izuzu switch||||1||
Z||000000||fiero56||08-15-2000||12:34 AM||||With colder temps approaching, I think I will take out this stupid Getrag with bad 2nd and 3rd gear syncros from my '88 Formula and replace it with an Izuzu tranny from a 4-cyl. As the temps get colder, the tranny oil stays thicker, making stiffer shifting, and lots of grinding in my tranny, and I don't feel like taking the time and expense of rebuilding it right now.<P>Question is this, will the shift and select cable routing have to be changed for the Izuzu, or can I keep the exisiting setup, and just change out the tranny? Also, will I have to change the tranny mounts, or will the current Getrag mounts work just fine? ||||reg||1
Z||000001||fiero56||08-15-2000||12:57 AM||||Ah crap! My ingenious plan has a few problems. First, I will have to use an Izuzu clutch set, the slave and master cylinders might be different. Everything on mine is only 15,000+ miles. Maybe I will just live with my current Getrag, or use a FWD getrag from another car. Rodney, can I use the same clutch set, and SC and MC?||||reg||1
Z||000002||Rodney||08-15-2000||08:12 AM||||I'm not sure on the clutch but I do believe you do have to use the 4 cylinder one. The masters are all the same in the piston diameter for all years. So that is OK to leave. You will need an Isuzu slave. The Getrag slave has a larger diameter bore. The push rods are also different in lenght between them.||||reg||1
Z||000003||TheFiero64||08-15-2000||02:47 PM||||I have the Izuzu trans with my v6. I used the clutch from the v6 4speed. Everthing else is from the Izuzu and it works great.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/TheFiero64_signature1.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||fiero56||08-15-2000||03:41 PM||||So if I were to pick up an Izuzu, I could use the same clutch I have coupled with my Getrag right now? What about shift and select cables? Are they the same? What about cable routing? Tranny mounts, will my current Getrag mounts hook right up to the Izuzu?||||reg||1
Z||000005||pherder||08-15-2000||06:39 PM||||fiero56,<P>Cables are different, throwout bearing is different, clutch slave is different, the metal brackets that attach the transaxle to the rubber trans mounts are different, the route the cables take is different (both of the Isuzu cables go up and over and down to the transaxle ... the Muncie has one that comes up from underneight.  <P>I have both and have been swapping and cursing ...<P>Paul||||reg||1
